geforce-sriov: the host driver accepts the programs of NVIDIA's second package, and only those.

Every NVIDIA library opens /dev/nvidiactl and sends NV_ESC_CHECK_VERSION_STR with its own version string.
The host package's driver (580.159.01) compares it with its own, byte for byte. The libraries of the second
package (580.159.03) are the same code for the same major version, and NVIDIA's own check has a relaxed
form, which compares the strings up to the first decimal point and is what the libraries ask for when
__RM_NO_VERSION_CHECK is in their environment.

A strict request whose version string is exactly the second package's version is passed to that check as a
relaxed one, and the reply is the one a strict success has (the request's cmd is put back). NVIDIA's check
still runs and still refuses another major version. A request of any other version string, including the
host's own (nvidia-smi, NVML, the vGPU manager), takes the path it took before.

The driver step replaces @GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT@ with the version of the second package before it applies this
patch, and only in a display build whose second package is not of the host's version. The string is also a
modinfo field of the built module (gs_client_accept), so the installed file says what it accepts.
Every hunk must match exactly once (gs_apply_source_patch); the line numbers are those of 580.159.01.

--- a/nvidia/nv.c
+++ b/nvidia/nv.c
@@ -964,1 +964,7 @@
+/* geforce-sriov: the version string of the second package's programs, which nvidia_ioctl accepts (see NV_ESC_CHECK_VERSION_STR). */
+#define GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT "@GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT@"
+MODULE_INFO(gs_client_accept, GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT);
+
 static void __exit nvidia_exit_module(void)
@@ -2587,8 +2593,22 @@
         case NV_ESC_CHECK_VERSION_STR:
         {
+            nv_ioctl_rm_api_version_t *gs_v = arg_copy;
+            NvBool gs_accept;
+
             NV_CTL_DEVICE_ONLY(nv);
 
+            /* geforce-sriov: a strict request of exactly the second package's version is checked as a relaxed one. */
+            gs_accept = arg_size == sizeof(*gs_v) && gs_v->cmd == NV_RM_API_VERSION_CMD_STRICT &&
+                        strnlen(gs_v->versionString, NV_RM_API_VERSION_STRING_LENGTH) == sizeof(GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT) - 1 &&
+                        memcmp(gs_v->versionString, GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT, sizeof(GS_CLIENT_ACCEPT)) == 0;
+            if (gs_accept)
+                gs_v->cmd = NV_RM_API_VERSION_CMD_RELAXED;
             rmStatus = rm_perform_version_check(sp, arg_copy, arg_size);
+            if (gs_accept)
+                gs_v->cmd = NV_RM_API_VERSION_CMD_STRICT;
             status = ((rmStatus == NV_OK) ? 0 : -EINVAL);
             break;
         }
